# Build-context excludes for when THIS checkout is a Docker build context root.
#
# That is the case for an outside image that embeds llmd and passes this
# checkout in as a named context (`docker build --build-context llmd=../llmd`).
# BuildKit honours a named context's own .dockerignore, and what is listed here is never sent to the
# builder at all — unlike `COPY --exclude`, which filters only after the whole
# directory (node_modules included, ~800 MB) has been transferred.
#
# llmd's own Dockerfile.linux-* build from the PARENT directory
# (`cd .. && docker buildx build -f llmd/Dockerfile.linux-amd64 .`), so this file
# does not apply to them.
#
# Such an image takes two things from here: the Go module (compiled into the
# host binary via a go.mod replace) and packages/{client,core,react} INCLUDING
# their built dist/ (npm-packed into its web build). Do not exclude dist, and do
# not exclude anything a non-test //go:embed reads: cmd/llmd/debugserver/assets/,
# internal/knowledge/db/migrations/*.sql,
# internal/llm/claudecode/claude_base_models.json.

# VCS and CI
.git
.github

# JS dependencies — the image installs its own.
**/node_modules

# Working state that changes on its own (editor and agent tooling writes
# .konstruct*; sqlite changes whenever anything opens it). Left in, these bust the image's Go layers.
**/.konstruct*
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite-*

# Caches, reports, docs, fixtures — read by no build stage.
.vite
e2e-reports
**/e2e
docs
**/testdata
tmp
*.out
*.log

# Host-built binaries (see .gitignore) — the image builds its own. `**/` because
# unlike .gitignore, a .dockerignore pattern is anchored at the context root:
# a bare `llmd-embed-example` missed examples/embed/llmd-embed-example, which
# alone was tens of MB per transfer.
/llmd
cmd/llmd/llmd
**/llmd-linux-*
**/llmd.exe
**/llmd-e2e-bin
**/llmd-embed-example

# Local config that may hold credentials, and scratch notes.
providers.yaml
llmd-followups.md
